{"id":"_summary","shard":"Bikes-03","checked":300,"ok":220,"issues":80,"by_kind":{"facets":35,"category":12,"brand":12,"name":11,"junk":10,"variant":9,"duplicate":4},"high":38,"rule_gaps":["Bikes `type` derivation defaults to Drivetrain for Shimano/SRAM part names: skivebrems*/bremse*/felgbrems sets, hjul/nav/hjullager (wheel + hub parts) and sykkelsko all land on Drivetrain instead of Brakes/Wheels/Apparel — 24 rows in this shard alone","'piggdekk' (studded winter tyre) is not matched by the dekk -> 'Tyres & tubes' rule, so studded tyres derive no type","apparel nouns (sokker, bukse, hettegenser, baselag*, sykkelsko) never derive type=Apparel, and lights (lykt/lys/baklys) never derive type=Accessories — absent across the whole shard, not per-row","wheel size is not derived when the inch mark is HTML-escaped ('26&quot;') or written with a comma decimal and no quote ('27,5A40')","srcCat 'Kondisjon / Treningssykkel' and 'Kondisjon / Spinningsykkel' resolve to Bikes; stationary exercise/spin bikes should route to Sport","Sport 1 / Intersport / Jernia feeds publish ALL-CAPS brands (SCOTT, SYNCROS, GIRO, CONTINENTAL, SWEET PROTECTION, WELDTITE) and legal entities ('Thule Sweden AB'), splitting the brand facet against the same brands from other shops"],"notes":"Healthy shard overall: ~85% of rows are correctly categorised bike components from one shop (Bikeshop). The dominant defect is the derived `type` facet, not `cat` — every disc brake, wheel, hub and cycling shoe from the Shimano/SRAM naming pattern is typed Drivetrain. Secondary: eight non-bike goods (sleeping pads, water filter, swim shoes, base layers) inherited Bikes from a bike shop's feed with no srcCat, and four exercise/spin bikes from Sporttema belong in Sport. 152 of 300 rows still have no image, which is the sampled-crawl state rather than a per-row fault."}
